22a417f29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446731 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446731 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107986" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446731 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446731 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 5 & -10\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446731 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0b0fd647-11bd-5cf6-9bab-c8f19524ee42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446731 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & -7 \\\\ 5 & -10-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & -7 \\\\ 5 & -10-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-10-\\lambda )-5\\cdot (-7) & =0 \\\\ -20-2\\lambda +10\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+35 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +15 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446732 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446732 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107982" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446732 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446732 #edb/ref 1071 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix \n$P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446732 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0d05d968-12a6-5808-b925-0cd007f4210b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446732 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by writing the matrix $P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(P-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 4 & =0 \\\\ 3-\\lambda -3\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-8 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot (-5)}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{36}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 6}{2} \\\\  & =5,-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-1$ and $\\lambda =5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446733 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446733 #edb/ref 1069 "q-76363" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446733 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446733 #edb/ref 1071 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$M=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{13} & \\sqrt{17} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446733 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "463f0d10-4286-59ff-a21d-e7909700880b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446733 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by writing the matrix $M-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nM-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{13}-\\lambda  & \\sqrt{17} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(M-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{13}-\\lambda  & \\sqrt{17} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (\\sqrt{13}-\\lambda )(\\frac{1}{2}-\\lambda )-0\\cdot \\sqrt{17} & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -\\sqrt{13})(\\lambda -\\frac{1}{2}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =\\sqrt{13}$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446734 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446734 #edb/ref 1069 "q-106996" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446734 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446734 #edb/ref 1071 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$C=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446734 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4f368600-216e-5acd-8869-df093ce09e0f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446734 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by writing the matrix $C-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nC-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(C-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -7)(\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =7$ and $\\lambda =-2.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446735 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446735 #edb/ref 1069 "q-76342" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446735 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446735 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix $M=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446735 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "548202ea-0779-523d-b823-a5921b15b56b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446735 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,M-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nM-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda  & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda  & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-0\\cdot \\sqrt{7} & =0 \\\\ (\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda ) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446736 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446736 #edb/ref 1069 "q-12298" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446736 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446736 #edb/ref 1071 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$U=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446736 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "649da0b4-9af9-52b6-817f-cca5e0eb449f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446736 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by writing the matrix $U-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nU-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 4 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(U-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 4 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-2-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda )-5\\cdot 4 & =0 \\\\ 6+2\\lambda +3\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-20 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+5\\lambda -14 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-5\\pm \\sqrt{{5}^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 14}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5\\pm \\sqrt{81}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5\\pm 9}{2} \\\\  & =-7,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-7$ and $\\lambda =2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446737 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446737 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36772" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446737 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446737 #edb/ref 1071 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$L=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ -9 & -11\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446737 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "688b15c3-44c2-5c91-89ca-dd25252cd049" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446737 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by writing the matrix $L-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nL-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ -9 & -11-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(L-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(L-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ -9 & -11-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(-11-\\lambda )-6\\cdot (-9) & =0 \\\\ -33-3\\lambda +11\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+54 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +21 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={8}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 21 \\\\  & =64-84 \\\\  & =-20 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $L$ does not have real eigenvalues." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446738 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446738 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36781" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446738 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446738 #edb/ref 1071 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$U=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -7\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446738 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6ff2d918-34fd-53ce-9a32-6157ad95bf62" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446738 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by writing the matrix $U-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nU-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-7-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ -1 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(U-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-7-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ -1 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-7-\\lambda )(-7-\\lambda )-5\\cdot (-1) & =0 \\\\ 49+7\\lambda +7\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+5 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+14\\lambda +54 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={14}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 54 \\\\  & =196-216 \\\\  & =-20 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $U$ does not have real eigen