da  & -9 \\\\ 2 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda )-2\\cdot (-9) & =0 \\\\ -12-4\\lambda +3\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+18 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda +6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-1)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =1-24 \\\\  & =-23 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $Q$ does not have real eigenvalues." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446741 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446741 #edb/ref 1069 "q-106954" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446741 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446741 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446741 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8a11188a-8a0f-5ab5-9de2-8d85b1d9c9bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446741 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-2\\cdot (-2) & =0 \\\\ 4-\\lambda -4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446742 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446742 #edb/ref 1069 "q-12293" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446742 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446742 #edb/ref 1071 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix \n$P=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446742 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "95ae8df3-3e